1. What is Immutability?

Immutability means once a value is created, it cannot be changed. Instead of modifying the existing data, we create a new copy with the changes.

Mutable Example ❌
let user = {
    name: "Sarju",
    age: 21
};

user.age = 22;

console.log(user);

Output:

{
  name: "Sarju",
  age: 22
}

Here the original object itself was modified.